<title>ARGENTINA: Chirac arrives in Argentina for two-day trade visit.</title>
<headline>Chirac arrives in Argentina for two-day trade visit.</headline>
<dateline>BUENOS AIRES 1997-03-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>French President Jacques Chirac arrived in Buenos Aires late on Sunday for a two-day visit during which he will seek to boost trade and investment ties with Argentina and its south American partners.</p>
<p>Chirac has proposed cementing ties between the European Union and the Mercosur customs union, which comprises Argentina, Brazil, Paraguay and Uruguay.</p>
<p>The French leader, who is travelling with 20 leading businessmen, included in his tour all four Mercosur members plus Bolivia, which has a free trade deal with the group.</p>
<p>On Monday he plans to meet Argentine President Carlos Menem and have lunch with Argentine and French businessmen.</p>
<p>On Tuesday he will visit Congress and meet members of the French community in Argentina before returning to Paris in the afternoon.</p>
</text>
